{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Before anything is built, storyboard the film the way an editor does. Send the storyboard you drafted from plan_video: 1 direction for a fixed brief, 2\u20134 when it's open. Each direction: logline, references (REF id + the one job each does), palette, type, sound, 2\u20133 style frames at full look, and 3\u201330 numbered panels in order, each with in/out seconds, shot size, camera move, action, VO, on-screen text, sound, the transition into the next panel, and its frame as layers (text, REF stills or the user's own captures by https URL, and shapes; positions in % of the frame). Mark a layer real only when it's a real capture of the user's product or a real result. This checks the timing and the REF ids and returns each REF's real still. While it returns ok: false it lists what to fix (fix it and call again); with ok: true it tells you how to lay the storyboard out as a Claude Design canvas (or as a text board where you can't make one). Free with Pro. Let the user pick a direction before you write any build prompt.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","properties":{"aspect":{"enum":["16:9","9:16","1:1","4:5"],"type":"string"},"bpm":{"maximum":220,"minimum":40,"type":"number"},"brand":{"description":"Brandprint import used for the look, if any","maxLength":80,"type":"string"},"brief":{"maxLength":1200,"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"directions":{"items":{"properties":{"logline":{"description":"the idea in one line","maxLength":280,"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"motion":{"description":"how frames hand off to each other overall","maxLength":400,"type":"string"},"name":{"maxLength":60,"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"palette":{"items":{"pattern":"^#([0-9a-fA-F]{3}|[0-9a-fA-F]{6}|[0-9a-fA-F]{8})$","type":"string"},"maxItems":8,"type":"array"},"panels":{"items":{"properties":{"action":{"description":"what happens an